{{smaller block|'''Aden''' or '''Aleppo ulcer''', a cutaneous affection occurring in the East, which, beginning as a small red papule, grows, suppurates, and finally ulcerates. The etiology is obscure, and apparently there has been great freedom in the application of the name to skin-diseases of this type when occurring in the East. There seems to be no essential difference in the meaning of the following terms: ''Delhi boil, Aleppo evil, Aleppo boil, Aleppo gall, Biskra button, Pendjeh ulcer, Delhi sore, Oriental sore, Persian ulcer,'' and many others qualified by the name of some Eastern town or country. They are all classed under the one name ''endemic ulcer.''—'''Perforating ulcer of the foot.''' See ''perforating.''—'''Varicose ulcer.''' See ''varicose.''—'''Warty ulcer.''' See ''warty.''}}

