'''ulema''' (ö′le-mä), ''n.'' [= F. ''uléma, oulema'' = Sp. ''ulema,'' < Ar. ''‘ūlemā,'' pl. of ''‘ālim,'' learned, one who knows, < ''‘alama,'' know: see ''alma.''] The Moslem doctors of sacred law and theological science, especially those belonging to the religious hierarchy of the Turkish empire, with the Sheik ul Islam at their head: a collective term.

'''ule-tree''' (ū′le-trē), ''n.'' A Mexican tree, ''Castilloa elastica,'' from the milky juice of which caoutchouc is obtained. See cut under ''Castilloa.''

